1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,880
Quarantine. Proof, not claims. Every pip
install runs someone else's code before
anyone has read it. This one runs it inside a
container that cannot reach the network,
cannot write outside its folder, and does not
have root — and then shows you what it tried.

2
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:19,160
Five runs, three packages, one of them
blocked.

3
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:33,810
harborline 2.9.1. The model read it, chose
which probes to run, and executed them on a
Vultr VM. Verdict: high. And the sentence that
matters is the first one — the package builds
and imports cleanly.

4
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:53,550
Because the problem is not in the package. It
pins urllib3 1.24.1, a release from 2018:
thirteen known advisories, the worst scored
eight out of ten. The block threshold is
seven, so this stops here. The wheels are
fetched and hashed, never installed — that
hash is what you would actually get.

5
00:00:54,350 --> 00:01:10,430
The threshold is a setting, not a constant. So
is the model, the reasoning budget, and how
many runs one address may start per hour. And
the honest part: accounts are demo-only here,
and the delete button is deliberately inert,
because a delete button without authentication
would be a mistake.

6
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:25,990
Two runs earlier, the same package was fine.
2.9.0 and 2.8.0 both came back low — 2.9.0
with a note that one dependency was a minor
behind. The regression arrived with 2.9.1.

7
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:41,450
Every claim in this report points at a file:
the proxy log, the process result, the
filesystem diff. The model may summarise them.
It may not assert anything they do not contain
— a claim citing a source that is not in this
run is dropped, and you can see it here.

8
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:55,760
The architecture fits in three sentences: a VM
runs the control plane, every task gets its
own hardened container, and the verdict is
built from evidence the container cannot write
to. Source is public, MIT, ninety-six tests.

9
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:59,250
Quarantine. Live at this URL.
